WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:08.120
I'm going to attempt to classify all of artificial&nbsp;
intelligence or AI into seven types. And that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:13.360
a tall order. But these seven types of AI&nbsp;
can largely be understood by examining two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:21.920
encompassing categories. There's AI capabilities,&nbsp;
and there's AI functionalities. So let's start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:33.760
with AI capabilities, and there are three. The&nbsp;
first of which is known as artificial narrow AI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:42.240
which also goes by the rather unflattering name of&nbsp;
"weak AI". Now, on its face, that doesn't sound like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:49.840
a very interesting capability to start us off.&nbsp;
But actually, narrow AI is the only type of AI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:57.480
that exists today--it's all we currently have. Any&nbsp;
other form of AI is theoretical. So we can think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:06.320
of this as realized AI--that's the artificial&nbsp;
intelligence we have today. And theoretical AI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:12.680
which is the artificial intelligence we may have&nbsp;
in the future. And now narrow AI can be trained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:21.080
to perform a narrow task, which, to be fair&nbsp;
to narrow AI, might be something that a human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:28.360
could not do as well as the AI can. But it can't&nbsp;
perform outside of its defined task. It does need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:35.920
us humans still to train it. So if narrow AI&nbsp;
represents all AI capabilities we have today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:44.000
well, what else is there? Well, a favorite of&nbsp;
memes, science fiction, and betting markets is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:55.280
artificial general intelligence, also known as&nbsp;
AGI. And also known as "strong AI". To be clear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:03.200
AGI is currently nothing more than a theoretical&nbsp;
concept. But here's the idea: AGI can use previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:09.520
learnings and skills to accomplish new tasks&nbsp;
in a different context, without the need for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:17.000
us human beings to train the underlying models.&nbsp;
If AGI wants to learn how to perform a new task,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:23.280
it will figure it out by itself. Which&nbsp;
sounds... disconcerting. But, but look,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:34.040
we haven't even talked about the third type of AI&nbsp;
capability yet. And that's artificial "super AI". If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:41.880
ever realized, super AI would think, reason,&nbsp;
learn, make judgments and possess cognitive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:49.400
abilities that surpass those of human beings.&nbsp;
The application's [possessing] super AI capabilities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:55.000
would have evolved beyond the point of catering&nbsp;
to humans sentiments and experiences, and would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:04.120
able to feel emotions and have needs and possess&nbsp;
beliefs and desires of their own. Yeah. So let's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:11.280
park that cheery thought for now, and consider&nbsp;
the four types of AI based on functionalities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:18.640
And we're back in the real world of realized&nbsp;
AI here--at least initially. So we can think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:33.360
of narrow AI as having two fundamental functions.&nbsp;
One of those is reactive machine AI. Now reactive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:42.360
machine AI are systems designed to perform a very&nbsp;
specific specialized task. Reactive AI stems from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:49.240
statistical math, and it can analyze vast amounts&nbsp;
of data to produce a seemingly intelligent output.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:58.400
We've had reactive AI for quite a long time. Back&nbsp;
in the late 1990s, IBM's chess playing supercomputer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:04.680
Deep Blue beat chess grandmaster Garry Kasparov by&nbsp;
analyzing the pieces on the board and predicting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:10.840
the probable outcomes of each move. That's a&nbsp;
specialized task with a lot of available data&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:19.760
to create insights. The hallmark of reactive AI.&nbsp;
We can think of other narrow AI functionalities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:30.720
really as being classified as "limited memory&nbsp;
AI". Now this form of AI can recall past events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:37.960
and outcomes and monitor specific objects or&nbsp;
situations over time. It can use past and present&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:44.000
moment data to decide on a course of action most&nbsp;
likely to help achieve a desired outcome. And as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:50.240
it's trained on more data over time, limited&nbsp;
memory AI can improve in performance. Think of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:56.480
your favorite generative AI chatbot, which relies&nbsp;
on limited memory AI capabilities to predict the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:03.520
next word or the next phrase or the next visual&nbsp;
element within the context it's generating. Okay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:13.960
so what about our two theoretical AI capabilities?&nbsp;
Well, if we look at AGI, we have to think about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:24.720
"theory of mind AI". Now, this would understand&nbsp;
the thoughts and emotions of other entities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:31.840
specifically us, so it could infer human motives&nbsp;
and reasoning and personalize its interactions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:38.400
with individuals based on their unique emotional&nbsp;
needs and intentions. And actually, emotion AI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:44.720
is a theory of mind AI currently in development.&nbsp;
AI researchers hope it will have the ability to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:53.000
analyze voices, images and other kinds of data&nbsp;
to understand and respond to human feelings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.000 --> 00:06:04.120
Finally! An AI that really understands me. And&nbsp;
then finally, under super AI, we have "self-aware&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:13.480
AI". Winning my personal award for the scariest AI&nbsp;
of all, it would have the ability to understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:21.400
its own internal conditions and traits, leading to&nbsp;
its own set of emotions, needs and beliefs. Look,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:28.520
we've covered seven types of AI, and only three&nbsp;
of them actually exist today! There is still so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:34.960
much to be learned and discovered. But as&nbsp;
those advancements happen, at least here we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:49.440
have a taxonomy of AI types that will tell&nbsp;
us how far along we are on our AI journey.

